{#-
  Multi-model second-opinion dispatch loop (PLAN-second-opinion-multi-model ADR-011).

  Owns the `config.second_opinion.models` gating so an empty/absent config renders BYTE-ZERO
  (failures.md [fail:design] absent-case rule) — the per-model partials never self-gate.
  For each enabled model, includes the right per-model transport partial (codex / antigravity),
  each of which emits its own invoke + adapt + graceful-skip recipe.

  Callers set `second_opinion_stage` ("review" | "plan") and `is_codex` before the include.
  The `{%- ... %}` whitespace control keeps the disabled render byte-zero.
-#}
{%- set _so = (config.get('second_opinion', {})) if config else {} -%}
{%- set _models = _so.get('models', []) -%}
{%- if _models %}
{%- if _models | length >= 2 %}

> **⚡ Concurrency (≥2 models enabled).** The per-model recipes below are independent — each
> writes its own temp files and is graceful-degraded separately. Do **not** run them one at a time.
> Instead: (1) do the fast setup for **every** model first — the `mktemp` + the prompt-file `Write`
> for each; (2) then dispatch **every** model's invoker call (`… -m harness_maker.second_opinion_invoke …`) in a **single
> message as parallel Bash tool calls** — do not wait for one model's CLI to return before starting
> the next. **Substitute each model's literal printed temp-file paths** (from its own `mktemp`
> output) into its invoker call, NOT the shared `$prompt_tmp` shell variable: each Bash
> call is a fresh shell, and the per-model recipes reuse the same variable names, so a shared
> variable would resolve to the wrong model's file. (3) adapt each model's output as it returns and
> emit its `second_opinion_results` entry exactly as the per-model recipe specifies. Per-model
> skip/failure handling + ledger rows are unchanged — each parallel call is tracked independently.
{% endif %}
{%- if second_opinion_stage == 'review' %}

> **⏱️ Run the invoker in the BACKGROUND, so it overlaps Pass 1.** Every invoker call below is a
> Bash tool call — give it **`run_in_background: true`**, then dispatch the Pass 1 reviewer fan-out
> **without waiting**. Collect the invoker's JSON line when you need it, at the Step 4 filter.
>
> This is the mechanism the concurrency decision always assumed and never had. The instruction to
> run the cross-model call "concurrently with Pass 1" shipped as prose with nothing behind it —
> `run_in_background` appeared **nowhere** in this harness — so the foreground Bash blocked for up
> to `CODEX_TIMEOUT_S=300` before the first reviewer was even dispatched. Nothing in the cross-model
> path consumes Pass 1's output, which is why the overlap is safe rather than merely faster.
>
> **A render-grep for `run_in_background` is a precondition, never the proof.** Whether the call
> actually overlaps is a property of one real dispatch; fixture-shaped output proves the validator
> and never the producer.
{%- endif %}
{%- if second_opinion_stage == 'plan' %}

> **⏱️ Do NOT background the invoker at this stage.** `/hm:plan` must *inject* the adapted findings
> into the plan validator's prompt **before** dispatching it, so a backgrounded call would have
